{
  "_comment": "The tag vocabulary for scripts/tag-tracks.py. Edit freely: a tag is scored by CLAP against its prompts and, where `essentia` lists matching model classes, by those classes too. Prompts describe how the music sounds, not what a video is about. A class name ending in * matches every class with that prefix (the strongest of them counts). A tag with Essentia classes is only applied when both models rate the track above the catalog average, so a bad mapping makes a tag rarer, never noisier. Re-run tag-tracks.py after editing; the audio analysis is cached, so only the cheap scoring step repeats.",
